    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n109935" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑψηχ-ής</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ές</span>,
			(<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἦχος</span>) <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>making a loud</i> or <i>ringing sound,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑψηχέες ἵπποι,</span> because of their
				<i>loud neighing,</i> or their '<i>high-resounding pace</i>'
			(cf. <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἐρίγδουπος</span>), <i><span class="en">
				Il.
				5.772
			</span></i> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑψαύχενες</span>
			 ap.<i><span class="en">
				Longin.
			</span></i>), <i><span class="en">
				23.27
			</span></i>; 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">τὸ ὑ. τῶν λόγων</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Philostr.
					<u>VS</u>
					1.25.7
				</span></i>
			.</div>
